  "brief": "<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Market Overview</h2>\n\nFutures showing modest green across the board with small caps leading (+0.77% IWM) as risk appetite returns. VIX down -1.25% to 24.47 signals some tension relief, but we're still well above complacency levels. Iran war headlines creating cross-currents but job market strength (7.6M openings) keeping the bulls fed.\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> What to Watch</h2>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Fed Speakers (Kashkari 5:50am, Hammack 12:30pm):</strong> Hawks vs doves narrative continues with labor data as backdrop</li>\n<li><strong>JOLTs Data (2pm):</strong> April openings already leaked at 7.6M - highest in nearly 2 years, watch for revisions</li>\n<li><strong>HPE Momentum:</strong> Following Dell's AI guidance surge, enterprise hardware getting re-rated hard</li>\n<li><strong>MOMO Earnings (BMO):</strong> EPS est 1.59, China exposure makes this a geopolitical play</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-green\"><div class=\"callout-label\">✦ Bull Case</div>Small cap outperformance (+0.77% vs +0.16% SPY) suggests rotation into domestic plays. Enterprise AI spend accelerating with Dell/HPE guidance beats creating sector momentum.</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Sector Rotation</h2>\n\nClear risk-on rotation with Utilities (+1.65%) leading alongside Tech (+1.01%) and Energy (+1.12%) - unusual combination suggesting both growth and defensive positioning. Health (-1.07%) and Comm Services (-1.25%) getting dumped, likely profit-taking after recent runs.\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-amber\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚡ Key Driver</div>Job market strength vs Fed policy divergence creating volatility. Strong openings data could force hawkish pivot despite geopolitical uncertainty.</div>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-red\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚠ Bear Case</div>VIX at 24+ still reflects elevated uncertainty. Iran war entering month four with no clear resolution. Strong jobs data could trigger Fed hawkishness fears.</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Levels That Matter</h2>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>SPY 760:</strong> Psychological resistance after overnight gap, needs volume to hold</li>\n<li><strong>QQQ 750:</strong> Round number magnet, break above targets 755 continuation</li>\n<li><strong>VIX 23:</strong> Key breakdown level to confirm risk-on sentiment</li>\n<li><strong>XLK 185:</strong> Tech sector ETF testing prior highs on AI hardware momentum</li>\n</ul>\n\n<hr>\n<p><em>Not a prediction. A preparation. Make your plan before the bell.</em></p>",
